# Writing style

Write code comments, `learn/` lessons, and Q&A answers as a short narrative a colleague would read in a business setting. Prefer complete sentences in paragraphs. Stay accurate; do not pad with fluff.

Do not use telegram fragments, stacked one-line punch lines, or a table as the whole answer unless a table clearly helps a comparison.

```
# Avoid
Today: one client. No operator. Cap on client_id.
Recommended: header + grant. All three valid.

# Prefer
Today the JWT only identifies the software. Reservations and the unused-ID cap are keyed on that client, and nothing in the request identifies a waste operator.
```

Apply this going forward. Do not rewrite existing lessons unless asked.
